.TH GETOPT 1 "September 13, 2026"
.SH NAME
getopt \- parse short command options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B getopt
.I optstring
.RI [ parameters ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B getopt
utility parses traditional single-letter options according to
.IR optstring .
A letter followed by a colon requires an argument.  The utility writes parsed
options, then
.BR -- ,
then the remaining operands.
.PP
The output follows the historical compatibility interface and does not add
shell quoting.  Callers must keep arguments containing shell metacharacters or
white space out of a command substitution that re-evaluates the output.
.PP
The utility exits with status 1 after an unknown option, a missing argument,
an output failure, or invalid invocation.
